<HTML>
<HEAD>
   <TITLE>Help </TITLE>
   <META http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">
   <LINK href="helpStyle.css" rel="stylesheet" title="WebEnabled" type="text/css">
</HEAD>
<BODY>
   <TABLE width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
      <!-- Begin logos row - middle logo is instrument specific -->
      <TR bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
         <TD valign="MIDDLE" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="230" height="60">
            <IMG src="../image/agilent.gif" width="230" height="60" border="0" alt="Agilent">
         </TD>
         <TD valign="top" bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" height="60">
            <IMG src="../image/instrumentBanner.gif" alt=""></TD>
      </TR>
      <!-- End logos row -->
      <TR>
         <TD colspan="2" bgcolor="#336699" class="blue">
            <IMG src="../image/filltrans.gif" height="2" alt=""></TD>
      </TR>
   </TABLE>
   <H1>
      Current Network Configuration Help</H1>
   <P>
      The <B>Current Network Configuration</B> page lets you view the network settings of the
      <%=sModel%>
      &nbsp;oscilloscope. These settings configure the instrument to operate in your specific
      network environment. The web page that appears when the "Configure Network" navigation
      tab is clicked is the Current Network Configuration page. This page shows the current settings
      that are in effect. If you wish to modify a parameter, you must click the "Modify
      Configuration" button.
   </P>
   <P>
      The parameters on the Current Network Configuration page include:
   </P>
   <UL>
      <LI>Configuration mode
         <P>
            This shows whether network configuration parameters (IP Address, 
			Subnet Mask, and Default Gateway) are determined automatically 
			(using DHCP and Auto IP) or set 
			manually.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Dynamic DNS
         <P>
            This parameter shows whether Dynamic DNS is enabled. If your network 
			provides Dynamic DNS, this option lets the oscilloscope register its 
			hostname and use the DNS server for name resolution.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>NetBIOS
         <P>
            This parameter shows if NetBIOS Naming Service is enabled. NetBIOS is a peer-to-peer
            naming protocol which allows systems to have hostnames without the existence of
            centralized name servers. NetBIOS Naming Service is useful for isolated subnets
            or direct connections with a crossover cable.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Multicast DNS
         <P>
            This parameter shows whether Multicast DNS is enabled. This lets 
			the oscilloscope use Multicast DNS for name resolution on small 
			networks without a conventional DNS server.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Multicast DNS
         Description
         <P>
            This parameter shows the oscilloscope's Multicast DNS description.          </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>IP Address
         <P>
            This is the Internet Protocol (IP) address of the instrument. The IP address is
            used for all TCP/IP communications with the instrument. If the 
			Configuration mode is Automatic, the IP address was assigned by these means. If 
			the Configuration mode is Manual, the IP address shown on the Modify Configuration page was used.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Subnet Mask
         <P>
            This parameter is used to enable the instrument to determine if an IP Address is
            on the same local subnet as the
            <%=sModel%>
            &nbsp;itself. When an address is on a different subnet, all packets must be sent
            to a gateway. If the Configuration mode is Automatic, the subnet mask was assigned
            by these means. If the Configuration mode is Manual, the subnet mask shown on the Modify
            Configuration page was used.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Default Gateway
         <P>
            This is the IP address of the default subnet gateway that allows the instrument
            to communicate with systems that are not on the local subnet. Packets which are
            destined for a device not on the local subnet, as determined by the subnet mask
            setting, are sent to the default gateway. If the Configuration mode 
			is Automatic, the default gateway
            was assigned by the DHCP server. If the Configuration mode is Manual 
			or if DHCP was unavailable on the
            network, the default gateway shown on the Modify Configuration page was used.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>DHCP Server
         <P>
            TThis parameter shows the IP address of the DHCP server. It is only 
			displayed if the Configuration mode is Automatic and the instrument obtained its IP address from a DHCP server.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>DNS Server(s)
         <P>
            This parameter shows the IP address of the Domain Name System (DNS) server. This
            server provides a hostname given an IP Address for a LAN device based on entries
            in its DNS lookup table. If a DNS server was entered on the Modify Configuration
            page, then that DNS server is used. If a DNS server is not entered, and 
			the Configuration mode is Automatic, up to three of DNS servers may 
			have been returned by the DHCP server at power-on. If the DNS server 
			address is unknown or incorrect, then the instrument will be unable 
			to determine its name on the network. 
      </LI>
      <LI>Hostname
         <P>
            This parameter shows the Internet hostname for the instrument. Depending upon what
            type of servers that you have, you may be able to use this name to connect to the
            instrument. If this field is blank, then the instrument was unable to find its name.
            This may be because the DNS server address is unknown or incorrect.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Domain
         <P>
            This parameter shows the Internet domain for the instrument.
         </P>
      </LI>
<%If sModelSeries = "3000" OR sModelSeries = "2000" Then%>
      <LI>GPIB Control
         <P>
            This parameter is ON when a GPIB module is present.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>GPIB Address
         <P>
            This parameter shows the instrument's GPIB bus address. This address is used when
            transfers are made on the GPIB bus.
         </P>
      </LI>
<%End If%>
      <LI>USB Control
         <P>
            This parameter is ON when a USB device port is present.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>LAN Control
         <P>
            This parameter is ON when a LAN module is present.
         </P>
      </LI>
   </UL>
</BODY>
</HTML>
